From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: ggml-cuda: top-k for small k over long rows without CUB

The DFlash2 drafter takes the 16 best candidates of each drafted row over the full 131,072-entry vocabulary. Without
CUB the CUDA top-k only accepts rows of up to 1024 columns, and CUB's top-k is one launch per row. For k of 8, 16 or 32
over rows of at least 1024 columns (a multiple of 4, 16-byte aligned), one block per row now keeps each thread's k
largest values sorted in registers from coalesced float4 loads, then emits the row's top k in descending order through
k rounds of a block-wide argmax over the threads' list heads (ties: lower column first). Other shapes keep the existing
paths.

Upstream: candidate (needs test-backend-ops top-k cases with long rows).

